  "ablation_size_label": "size = 52,428,800 (and 6 benchmark sizes)",
  "takeaways": [
    "**Per-Thread FP32 + Cross-Thread FP64 + Last-Workgroup Ticket Write (Contest BUG-002):** Monte Carlo simulation (`5,000` random seeds at `N = 52.4M`) proved that widening every element to `double` in the hot loop is unnecessary: accumulating in `float32` per thread (`a0..a3`) and widening to `double` **once per thread** before workgroup reduction stays >100x inside `rtol=1e-5` (`max rel err = 9.48e-8`), whereas thousands of concurrent `atom.global.add.f32` fail on 5.8% of seeds. Combining this with a persistent 16-byte scratch tensor (`double partial` + `uint ticket`) and last-workgroup ticket write eliminated all per-call PyTorch host launches (`torch::zeros` and `.to(kFloat32)`), cutting latency from `89.44 µs` to **`49.69 µs` on B200** (`4.22 TB/s`), `101.01 µs` to **`82.81 µs` on H100** (`2.53 TB/s`), `164.36 µs` to **`144.77 µs` on A100** (`1.45 TB/s`), and `974.52 µs` to **`866.51 µs` on L4** (`242.0 GB/s`, Rank **#11 / 43**).",
    "**Endeavour 192 Cache Hints (`:cache (:streaming :prefetch 256)`) & Read-Only `&out` (`.nc`):** Declaring `input` before `&out` with `:cache (:streaming :prefetch 256)` emits `ld.global.cs.nc.L2::256B.v4.f32` (non-coherent read-only + evict-first streaming + 256-byte L2 sector prefetch) and `(declare (unroll 8))`. On **H100**, **A100**, and **L4** (where the 209.7 MB input overflows the 40–50 MB L2 cache), `crisp_vectorsum_lastman_u8_cs256` improved `52.4M` benchmark latency to **`80.9–82.5 µs` on H100** and achieved our best leaderboard geomeans on **H100 (`82.81 µs` public / `82.68 µs` secret, Rank #32/67, `82.0%` of #1)**, **A100 (`144.77 µs` public / `146.15 µs` secret, Rank #63/114)**, and **L4 (`866.51 µs` public / `866.30 µs` secret, Rank #11/43, `79.9%` of #1, `94.3%` of #2 `816.29 µs`)**.",
    "**Contiguous 32 KB Block-Tiling (`tile8_fastwg`) & Single-Barrier Workgroup Reduction:** On H100 `N = 52.4M` benchmark mode, replacing runtime grid-stride indexing (`loop-vector-stride` with `(unroll 8)`, which requires 8 separate 64-bit stride registers and emits `.pragma \"nounroll\"`) with a persistent 32 KB contiguous-tile loop (`vectorsum_tile8_fastwg.crisp`) and single-barrier workgroup reduction (`bar.sync 0` + thread-0 8-way shared-memory sum) achieved the fastest single-case H100 benchmark time (**`81.3 ± 0.08 µs` mean, `80.1 µs` best**).",
    "**Compiler Codegen Finding — Inline PTX Displacement Folding:** In Endeavour 192 (`%ptx-hinted-load-lines` in `src/compiler.lisp`), each cache-hinted load is lowered to an LLVM inline `asm sideeffect \"ld.global... [$4]\"` call taking a single pointer register (`\"l\"(ptr)`). Because the pointer is opaque to LLVM's NVPTX address-mode matcher, constant byte displacements (`+4096 .. +28672` or `-12`) cannot be folded into `[%rd+OFFSET]` and instead materialize 7 extra `add.s64` instructions and 7 extra 64-bit registers per unrolled iteration. Teaching `%apply-cache-hints-to-ll` to fold constant `getelementptr` byte offsets into the inline PTX `[%rd+IMM]` addressing mode will eliminate those extra registers and `add.s64` instructions."
  ],
